## Example incident (anonymised)

A login page on Android shipped with a custom title bar showing the back button as `<` (chevron-left), font size 18sp, no shadow. The project's `AppTopBar` scaffold renders back as a circular icon, font 22sp, with a subtle bottom shadow. Three other pages had similar one-offs over the previous quarter. A coordinator UI audit caught the drift; a single architectural task replaced all four with `AppTopBar`, saving ~200 lines of duplicated code and bringing the app visually consistent. The audit also retroactively added the missing scaffold contract doc.
